What is derived, and what is not:

  * FLUI takes Flutter's observable behavior as its reference. Where a Flutter
    test pins that behavior, the scenario (inputs, expected values, edge
    cases) is adapted into a Rust test; each such file names its source in a
    "Ported from `.flutter/packages/flutter/...`" comment. As of 2026-09-03
    those files live in the crates flui-app, flui-foundation,
    flui-interaction, flui-objects, flui-rendering, flui-scheduler,
    flui-semantics, flui-testing, flui-view, and flui-widgets; a copy of this
    NOTICE ships with each of them.
  * Framework source is designed in Rust from that behavioral reference. It
    is not a translation of Dart source, and Flutter's documentation prose is
    not copied.

